<title>GERMANY: KOEBNICK SEES 6-8 EMU MEMBERS AS BEST SOLUTION.</title>
<headline>KOEBNICK SEES 6-8 EMU MEMBERS AS BEST SOLUTION.</headline>
<dateline>MAINZ, Germany 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Hans-Juergen Koebnick said on Wednesday the &quot;best solution&quot; to the problems surrounding the start of European monetary union would be a punctual start with a medium-sized group.</p>
<p>&quot;I still regard it as the best solution if EMU could start in 1999, initially with a core of six to eight countries whose currencies have in the past proven a high degree of internal and external stability and also do so for the future,&quot; he told a news conference.</p>
<p>&quot;That would be the best way to transfer the confidence of the mark to the euro,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
